  bcf-naming-generalization: the shipped K-forest amplitude family is
    spelled with BCF names at every layer - BCFSpec, BCFForestSpec,
    BCFState, BCFForestCombiner, BCFSpecStorage, createBCFSampler,
    ChainStateData::hasBCF and the state format's "bcf" block - so each
    reads "BCF" where it means "carries amplitudes". The debt and its
    mitigation (every capability probe is totalAmplitudes() != 0, never
    a name or a forest count) are described in
    docs/design/multiplier-combiner.md. BCFSpecStorage
    (R_interface_bartcore.cpp:2128; used at :2165, :2233, :2262, :2953,
    :3095) is the per-build backing store whose vectors a BCFSpec's
    pointers borrow - each forest's column subset, interaction pairs,
    block partition and transposed basis - one more BCF-prefixed name
    for the same general capability. The R side carries the identical
    tell: isBCFSampler (R/bartcore.R:24) and refuseBCFMutation
    (R/bartcore.R:34), the latter's five call sites R/bartcore.R:306,
    :327, :404 and R/dbarts.R:1161, :1622, every one of which reads or
    gates on data@bases rather than a forest count or a name. A rename
    is ENGINE work, not a docs edit: a --preclean, a structSize move on
    the state fixtures
    (common.cpp already tripped once, 272 -> 344), and a state-block key
    change needing the same in-place re-encode M4.3 used. The formerly listed
    user-visible leg (calibrationMapName's two-forest literal reaching
    setForestPriorScale's refusal) landed on its own; only the rename
    remains here. Pre-release, unscheduled.
  bcf-sigma-tail-mixing: OPTIONAL research door (docs/plans/bcf-sigma-
    residual.md sec 4 item 2; no separate plan doc). Open: the EXTREME
    tail (|a0| >= ~40, ~3% of the prior) is frozen-structure mixing
    that no amount of burn fixes; a principled remedy would target
    tree-structure mixing at high SNR (tempered early sweeps,
    restart-style grow proposals). Low priority - the regime only
    arises with a stale build scale swapped against a new response
    inside a larger Gibbs loop (setResponse updateScale=FALSE).
    research-open, decision-gated.
  binary-kforest-k1-reachability: K = 1 as a SHIPPED multi-forest
    configuration - one varying-coefficient forest with no prognostic
    partner, which is VCBART's shape (D4 of docs/design/model-space-
    survey.md). Today it is a designed refusal (spec.R, added by
    binary-kforest-prior-default S2). Priced live rather than
    inherited: the engine already takes it - drawGlue dispatches
    K != 2 to the general drawAmplitudes, synthesizeIndicatorBasis is
    gated on numForests_ > 1, shippedShape() is simply false at K = 1,
    and createBCFSampler imposes no count floor - so this is a bridge
    (applyBCFSpec's Rf_xlength < 2) plus R change with tests, NOT
    engine work. Gated on ACCEPTANCE EVIDENCE: a new shipped
    configuration owes its own, which is why S2 refused rather than
    opened it.
