  latent-family-weight-channel: ADJUDICATED 2026-08-15 (r-c-division
    census item G4, the one item the arc's itemization never
    scheduled): PARTIAL BUILD. Logistic weights are observation counts
    and the Polya-Gamma shape depends on them
    (LogisticResponse::refreshLatents sums lround(weights_[i]) PG(1,
    psi) draws), so a weight change is a model change with a defined
    meaning and an outer sampler that cannot make it cannot vary
    exposure; refuseBinaryWeightChange refuses it today. BUILD for
    logistic: relax the refusal, refresh the latents against the new
    counts on the swap (a stale omega is a wrong draw, not just a
    stale one), keep the positive-integer validation on the mutation
    path. DECLINE BY IDENTIFICATION for probit, ordinal, aft and
    nbinom - no weighted latent form, a creation-fixed censoring
    structure, and a y_i + r shape with no weight slot respectively -
    and say so in the weights item of man/dbartsSampler-class.Rd
    rather than leaving it an accident. Record in
    docs/design/r-c-division.md, "The latent-family weight channel".
    Memo price ~40 engine + ~60 test, to be re-derived in raw
    additions at scoping. OUTSIDE the adoption-slate arc;
    unscheduled, pre-release at discretion.
