  multinomial-counts-mutation: multinomial BART cannot mutate its
    RESPONSE side - alone among the families it cannot serve as a
    conditional inside a larger Gibbs sampler. The response is the
    combiner-owned counts_ matrix, so the content is a new COUNTS and
    n x K OFFSET channel plus creation-side surface. Enables
    competing-risks discrete-time hazard (moves with
    survival-followups), nominal-response IRT and discrete choice,
    SUR-style composition past the multinomial boundary. The
    predictor channel is already open; the gap is response-side only.
    COMPLETE 2026-08-12 (S1-S5; docs/plans/multinomial-counts-
    mutation.md). The multinomial family is now a full conditional
    inside a larger Gibbs/MH sampler. Open: no test-side
    bartcoreForestFits analog; ConfigSpec OP_SET_COUNTS rides the
    general multi-forest fuzz-arm gap.
  negbin-real-dispersion: recorded door out of the negative-binomial
    landing (docs/plans/negative-binomial.md; design sec 2 carries fork
    B's spec). Real-valued dispersion needs a non-integer-shape
    Polya-Gamma draw, for which no exact sampler exists, so shipping it
    means dbarts' first documented-approximate family (truncated
    gamma-sum, bias bounded ~1e-3 at K = 200) behind an explicit
    opt-in; the same decision gates weighted-binary's fractional
    weights. The engine seams are in place. Poisson family and grouped
    NB are companion doors (design sec 7). decision-gated.
  ordinal-scan-missing-rows: the grow-from-root ordinal scan drops
    missing rows from the split likelihood (scan.hpp skips naCode)
    while the no-split term counts them (grow.hpp takes the full
    node's stats), so a split score is short the missing rows' leaf
    marginal - the SECOND inconsistency the categorical-scan S0a
    falsifier surfaced and its verifier confirmed from code
    (2026-08-12; docs/plans/grow-from-root-categorical-scan.md S0a
    landing note). Two components: the dropped weighted
    sum-of-squares no longer cancels split-vs-no-split (monotone in
    the missing rows' sum w y^2: TV 0.017 -> 0.59 as it goes 0 ->
    32), and the missing weight never inflates child precision (the
    floor). Independent of the log 2 fork - 39 percent of the
    shipped-to-exact gap survives that fix. Opt-in grow path only,
    missing-bearing ordinal columns only. Own slice, draw-law
    change when taken.
